lobo dev
Rent an RTX 5090 on RunPod or Vast.ai and serve Qwen3.5-27B behind an OpenAI-compatible API.
Pods delete themselves when idle or expired.

Run
  up           Rent a 5090 and boot lobo; shows progress until the API is ready
  status       Live dashboard of the running pod
  logs         Print the pod's recent agent, llama-server and cloudflared logs
  test         Smoke test the live API: streamed chat + tool call
  down         Delete every lobo pod on every provider

Setup
  config       Set API keys and defaults for `lobo up` (form in a terminal)
  gen-api-key  Create LOBO_API_KEY in the config once (kept across ups) and write opencode.lobo.json with it
  version      Print version, commit and build date

Examples
  lobo config                   set API keys and defaults (first run)
  lobo up                       rent a 5090 and boot the model; live progress
  lobo up --provider vast       rent on Vast.ai instead of the default provider
  lobo up --q6 --min-mbps 200   smaller model, drop hosts slower than 200 MB/s
  lobo status                   live dashboard: GPU, tokens/s, idle timer, cost
  lobo down                     delete every lobo pod on every provider

Config
  /home/u/.config/lobo/config.env
  plain KEY=value lines: edit by hand or with `lobo config`; flags override its defaults

`lobo <command> --help` for flags.
